an has outraised the incumbent and holds a cash edge with no outside spending against her", "Thin, dated polling (one July LV poll) leaves real uncertainty about the true margin", "Miller-Meeks benefits from incumbency and a Trump-backed steel plant announcement in the district"], "rationale": "The evidence points toward a Democratic edge: eight of ten raters mark this a flip with a consensus Lean D, prediction markets give Bohannan roughly 82-85%, and she has matched the incumbent's fundraising while holding more cash. The only recent poll shows her up five, though its age and thinness keep uncertainty wide.", "watch": "A strong debate performance by Miller-Meeks or the steel plant story boosting Republican turnout could tighten the race.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["Newest usable poll is 78 days old; polling uncertainty inflated.", "Incumbent Mariannette Miller-Meeks (R) is running."]}, "overview": "Iowa's 1st District is a rematch between Republican incumbent Mariannette Miller-Meeks and Democrat Christina Bohannan in a seat with a modest Republican lean. Most nonpartisan and partisan raters alike now frame the race as a Democratic flip opportunity, ranging from Tilt D to Likely D, and prediction markets price Bohannan's chances in the low-to-mid 80s. Bohannan has raised about $7.1 million and holds a cash advantage, while outside spending against her has been minimal so far.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.7001, "margin": 3.17}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.7846, "margin": 4.5}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.8086, "margin": 5.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.8054, "margin": 5.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.7184, "margin": 4.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.759, "margin": 5.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.7744, "margin": 4.5}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.7867, "margin": 4.5}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.7982, "margin": 5.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.8113, "margin": 5.0}, {"date": "2026-1